    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation keyed on the `Idempotency-Key` header. When a create repeats with an already-seen key, the originally created owner is returned with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise 409).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the optional `Idempotency-Key` header parameter and a `200` response to the `addOwner` operation. Since this project generates its API interfaces from the spec, the generator now exposes the header as a `@RequestHeader(value = \"Idempotency-Key\", required = false)` argument on `OwnersApi.addOwner(...)`.\n\n2. **`OwnerCreationIdempotencyStore.java`** (new) \u2014 A small, single-responsibility `@Component` that remembers which owner id was produced for each key (`ConcurrentHashMap` behind `find`/`remember`).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 \n   - `addOwner` now takes the generated `idempotencyKey` parameter. If the key is present and already seen, it returns the stored owner with 200; otherwise it creates the owner, records the key\u2192id mapping, and returns 201 as before.\n   - Extracted all the create-time rule/validation/persist logic into a private `createOwner(...)` helper so the public method stays focused on the idempotency + response concern and the creation pipeline keeps its single responsibility.\n\nThe store is consulted *before* validation, so a repeat of identical data short-circuits ahead of the duplicate-owner check that would produce a 409.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `coreIdempotentRepeat` acceptance test), BUILD SUCCESS.",
