    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2192 `createOwner`), reading the code as it stands. I mark each step as **[V]** validation (can reject the request) or **[S]** side-effect (mutation, persistence, or logging).\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **[V] Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **[V] Request-body bean validation** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (from the generated `OwnersApi`). Enforced constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$\")`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$\")`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`; `address` \u2014 `@Size(1,255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`; `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid`\n\n## In `addOwner` (idempotency pre-check)\n\n3. **[S/short-circuit] Idempotency replay** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header has text and the `OwnerCreationIdempotencyStore` already maps it to an existing owner, that owner is returned with **200 OK** and creation is skipped entirely (none of the steps below run).\n\n## In `createOwner` (the create pipeline, in this exact order)\n\n4. **[S] Address normalization** \u2014 `AddressFormNormalizer.normalize` mutates the DTO: prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, normalizes each line via `AddressNormalizer`, and (re)composes the flat `address` (line1, plus `\" \" + line2` when a second line is present); otherwise normalizes the flat `address`.\n5. **[V] Required fields** \u2014 `OwnerRequestValidator.validate`: `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must each be non-null/non-blank \u2192 else `RequiredFieldsMissingException` naming every missing field.\n6. **[V] Postcode** \u2014 `PostcodeValidator.validate`: an absent postcode passes; if present it must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region the numeric value must fall within that region's inclusive range \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n7. **[V] City capacity** \u2014 `CityOwnerLimitValidator.validate`: rejects if the city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n8. **[V] Registration date not in future** \u2014 `RegistrationDateValidator.validate`: a supplied `registrationDate` after `LocalDate.now()` is rejected \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (null passes).\n9. **[V] Daily capacity** \u2014 `DailyOwnerLimitValidator.validate`: computes the business day (`BusinessDay.onOrAfter` of the supplied date, or today if none) and rejects if \u2265 100 owners already registered on that business day \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n10. **[S] Telephone normalization** \u2014 `TelephoneNormalizer.normalize` result is set back on the DTO: strips formatting, applies default country code `+61` (dropping a single leading `0`), produces E.164; **[V]** must be 8\u201315 digits and match the country's national length \u2192 else `InvalidTelephoneException` (null telephone also throws).\n11. **[S] Email normalization** \u2014 `EmailNormalizer.normalize` result set on the DTO: absent/blank \u2192 `null`; otherwise trimmed and lower-cased; **[V]** must match the email pattern \u2192 else `InvalidEmailException`.\n12. **[V] Disposable email** \u2014 `DisposableEmailDomainValidator.validate`: rejects if the (normalized) email's domain is in the blocklist `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (absent email passes).\n13. **[S] Map to entity** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` builds the `Owner`.\n14. **[S] Household id** \u2014 `owner.setHouseholdId(HouseholdIdGenerator.generate(lastName, postcode))` \u2014 first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 of the `(lastName, postcode)` household key.\n15. **Duplicate handling \u2014 branches on `sharesHousehold`:**\n    - If `sharesHousehold == true`: **[S]** set `possibleDuplicate = false`, `possibleDuplicateOf = null` (both duplicate checks bypassed).\n    - Else:\n      - **[V] Hard duplicate** \u2014 `DuplicateOwnerValidator.validate`: rejects if any non-deleted existing owner has the same `(lastName, postcode)` household key \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException`.\n      - **[S] Possible duplicate** \u2014 `PossibleDuplicateDetector.findPossibleDuplicate`: finds the lowest-id non-deleted owner with same last name + postcode but a different telephone; sets `possibleDuplicate` (true/false) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (that id or null).\n16. **[S] Customer code** \u2014 `owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCodeGenerator.generate(postcode, telephone, lastName))` \u2014 `\"<REGION>-<HASH8>\"`, de-duplicated against existing owners' codes by appending `-<n>` (n \u2265 2).\n17. **[S] Namesake count** \u2014 `owner.setNamesakeCount(clinicService.countNamesakes(firstName, lastName))`.\n18. **[S] Household size** \u2014 `owner.setHouseholdSize(HouseholdSizeCalculator.size(owner))` \u2014 1 plus every existing owner sharing the household key.\n19. **[S] Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (`@Transactional`, JPA `save`). On persist, the entity's `@PrePersist resolveRegistrationDate()` runs: **[S]** defaults `registrationDate` to today if null, then rolls it forward off weekends via `BusinessDay.onOrAfter`. (JPA/Hibernate bean-validation on the `Owner` entity \u2014 `@NotEmpty` on `address`/`city`/`telephone`, `@Pattern` E.164 on `telephone` \u2014 also applies at flush.)\n20. **[S] Audit log** \u2014 `OwnerAuditLogger.created(owner)` writes an `AUDIT` info line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber).\n\n## Back in `addOwner` (after `createOwner` returns)\n\n21. **[S] Remember idempotency key** \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header has text, `idempotencyStore.remember(key, owner.getId())`.\n22. **[S] Location header** \u2014 set to `/api/owners/{id}`.\n23. **[S] Response assembly** \u2014 `toOwnerDto(owner)` maps the entity and stamps `bulkSignupWarning` (true when > 80 owners already registered on today's business day, via `BulkSignupWarningEvaluator`); returns **201 CREATED**.\n\nA few things worth noting: the derived fields the audit log and response expose (`membershipLevel`/`membershipNumber`, `fiscalYear`, `checkDigit`, `ageBand`, `contactPreference`, `locality`, `timezone`, etc.) are computed on-read from stored fields, not persisted separately. Also, `DuplicateOwnerValidator` rejects on the household key `(lastName, postcode)` alone \u2014 it does not actually compare the full `identityKey` its Javadoc describes."
